{"version":"1","id":"shamundev","handle":"shamundev","name":"Ido Shamun","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/4df9590bfe494592ae55932a66d18369","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-8.7298,"y":8.5372,"cluster_id":2,"posts_collected":13,"newest_post_at":"2023-12-21T16:19:01.909Z","oldest_post_at":"2023-09-18T08:35:29.729Z","features":{"hype_score":0.0,"listicle_ratio":0.0,"question_ratio":0.0,"avg_read_time":3.461538,"summary_length_avg":307.615385,"title_length_avg":41.0,"title_length_var":163.692308,"tag_entropy":2.7581,"tag_diversity":1.384615,"top_tag_share":0.307692,"avg_upvotes":18.923077,"median_upvotes":10.0,"avg_comments":2.461538,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.133603,"zero_engagement_share":0.0,"viral_share":0.0,"posts_per_week":0.964764,"non_article_ratio":0.0,"author_present_share":1.0,"recency_skew":12.0},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[8.5735,9.0],"cadence_depth":[-9.2059,-5.8382],"hype_variety":[-5.2206,-4.3235],"title_style":[-5.1765,-2.2647]},"top_tags":[["startup",4],["leadership",3],["webdev",2],["javascript",2],["python",2],["architecture",1],["change-data-capture",1],["react",1]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["Engineering Handbook","The Journey of Becoming a CTO","Svelte Through the Eyes of a React Developer"],"outlier":["Client-Side-Servering: My Perspective on Next.js Server Actions"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"yh1E2HQg3","title":"Early Stage Startup Handbook","url":"https://shamun.dev/posts/startup-handbook","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/early-stage-startup-handbook-yh1e2hqg3","summary":"This post provides insights and strategies for scaling a startup, including routines and tools for effective communication, as well as the importance of documentation.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/5b092feff887eee95d3a0b612fd6993d?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":16,"num_comments":6,"created_at":"2023-12-21T16:19:01.909Z"},{"id":"r4RSrLOUh","title":"Type Safety for the Rest of Us","url":"https://shamun.dev/posts/type-safety","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/type-safety-for-the-rest-of-us-r4rsrlouh","summary":"Developing applications without types may provide a perceived feeling of speed, but it can lead to difficulties when onboarding new developers or maintaining code. Solutions such as TypeScript or tooling like JSDoc can help document code and improve maintainability.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/e9c2b4dd324397cff93b56ef47004257?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":25,"num_comments":4,"created_at":"2023-12-14T16:02:21.748Z"},{"id":"VdsbbZ0dG","title":"Engineering Handbook","url":"https://shamun.dev/posts/engineering-handbook","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/engineering-handbook-vdsbbz0dg","summary":"Daily.dev is creating an engineering handbook to streamline processes, normalize culture, and improve collaboration among engineers. The handbook includes sections on expectations, decision records, epic owner and individual contributor roles, communication preferences, and project management.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/7fe870fbeadc6758912ed0f89e456013?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":67,"num_comments":7,"created_at":"2023-12-02T19:04:20.698Z"},{"id":"D2tMcnD9v","title":"Svelte Through the Eyes of a React Developer","url":"https://shamun.dev/posts/svelte","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/svelte-through-the-eyes-of-a-react-developer-d2tmcnd9v","summary":"The author shares their experience transitioning from React to Svelte, discussing the differences in syntax, structure, and community size. They highlight the advantages of using SvelteKit for building applications and express intrigue in further exploring Svelte as a framework choice.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/575da75ad0408189b591ebdee1520521?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":29,"num_comments":5,"created_at":"2023-11-24T14:34:18.866Z"},{"id":"QyutnTuWk","title":"Designing Effective Interviews for New Roles in Startups","url":"https://shamun.dev/posts/effective-interviews","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/designing-effective-interviews-for-new-roles-in-startups-qyutntuwk","summary":"Learn how to design effective interviews for new roles in startups by converting the role's challenges into interview questions and focusing on expectations alignment, mutual fit, respect, and feedback.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/44636311b138adba24cd54c67af94250?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":4,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-11-15T10:43:36.931Z"},{"id":"HQAkgXdzk","title":"Ownership as the Key to Engineering Scalability","url":"https://shamun.dev/posts/ownership","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/ownership-as-the-key-to-engineering-scalability-hqakgxdzk","summary":"Empowering engineers with complete ownership of their projects from inception to completion is a key strategy for organizational scalability. This approach fosters professional growth, minimizes reliance on stakeholders, alleviates the burden on team leads, and enables fast-paced development. The role of feature lead, the creation of a Decision Record (DR), and the integration of DevOps responsibilities are key aspects of this approach.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/8493e311e1f528341b0d24a7227fe09c?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":5,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-11-10T16:40:03.289Z"},{"id":"mmEQUr4VV","title":"Client-Side-Servering: My Perspective on Next.js Server Actions","url":"https://shamun.dev/posts/client-side-servering","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/client-side-servering-my-perspective-on-next-js-server-actions-mmequr4vv","summary":"Server Actions in Next.js introduce a client-side-servering approach where the client code generates server endpoints. However, there are concerns about security, RPC implementation, reusability, vendor lock, and the learning curve for junior developers.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/b04f22b17d0d001b6a890926c38d409d?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":10,"num_comments":1,"created_at":"2023-11-01T11:26:03.686Z"},{"id":"KkbO4GxP5","title":"The Journey of Becoming a CTO","url":"https://shamun.dev/posts/cto-journey","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/the-journey-of-becoming-a-cto-kkbo4gxp5","summary":"The path to becoming a CTO is a journey that evolves along with the company's growth. It starts with coding and product work, then progresses to managing teams and bridging the gap between business and engineering. Lessons include focusing on exponential impact, setting aside time for coding, using prototypes for alignment, and hiring and documenting wisely. The role requires adaptability, flexibility, and continuous learning.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/4b8e413bfd0b6bc04d8a5e913c0d5cb0?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":58,"num_comments":2,"created_at":"2023-10-24T15:39:34.423Z"},{"id":"SHQQwwMMj","title":"CDC Changed the Way I Build Software","url":"https://shamun.dev/posts/cdc","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/cdc-changed-the-way-i-build-software-shqqwwmmj","summary":"Change Data Capture (CDC) is a design pattern used to monitor database changes and extend the reach beyond the database itself. It is important in software development as it simplifies the handling of distributed transactions and allows for more efficient and fault-tolerant systems. CDC changes the approach to building event-driven systems by offloading non-critical tasks to the background and optimizing performance.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/72bac13ed7256fd02b35116fc74f4b0c?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":4,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-10-18T12:52:56.580Z"},{"id":"mphODuORM","title":"Unleashing Vision with Prototyping","url":"https://shamun.dev/posts/prototyping","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/unleashing-vision-with-prototyping-mphoduorm","summary":"Prototyping is a powerful tool for CTOs to explore and bring their visionary ideas to life. It distills abstract ideas into clear concepts, provides stakeholders with a tangible platform for feedback, and allows for faster iteration using familiar tools and prebuilt UI components. Embracing prototyping helps unblock the flow of ideas and orchestrate progress.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/e5a74e59687b2152ba8e2af027ce1e2b?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":6,"num_comments":5,"created_at":"2023-10-10T15:09:52.017Z"}],"similar_handles":["nextaitool","microsaasexamples","frontend_developer","techgsmsoftwares","strapi_io"],"opposite_handles":["felixrieseberg","xai","hamelhusain","hwchase17","skirano"],"similar":[{"id":"e00b4499-9e40-4271-99c6-068a74910b4f","handle":"nextaitool","name":"Next AI Tool","is_squad":true,"x":-8.7236,"y":8.6017,"cluster_id":2,"posts_collected":80,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--ZKFJnCtH--/f_auto/v1727356536/squads/e00b4499-9e40-4271-99c6-068a74910b4f","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":4.779454,"median_upvotes":0.0,"author_present_share":1.0,"hype_score":0.00625,"avg_read_time":1.0375,"tag_diversity":1.0625},"top_tags_preview":[["ai",63],["machine-learning",15],["productivity",12]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-4.7059,10.0],"cadence_depth":[-1.5588,-9.1176],"hype_variety":[-0.6324,4.25],"title_style":[-6.1765,-4.0147]}},{"id":"7044f0c8-e4a2-46f7-afd5-9be2c8721e61","handle":"microsaasexamples","name":"Micro SaaS Examples","is_squad":true,"x":-8.642,"y":8.5489,"cluster_id":2,"posts_collected":72,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--9GQZKwI3--/f_auto/v1730836041/squads/7044f0c8-e4a2-46f7-afd5-9be2c8721e61","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":1.052187,"median_upvotes":0.0,"author_present_share":1.0,"hype_score":0.013889,"avg_read_time":2.25,"tag_diversity":1.319